What the final statements actually establish, read literally:

- theoremA: for the supplied P and M, if the listed published-rate, moment, and cost-interface propositions hold, then ∀ε>0, eventually M.factorCost N ≤ LN (1/2) (P.cA+ε) N. It neither constructs FACTOR nor states any output correctness.
- corollaryA: for a supplied family of models with the uniform-in-P hypotheses, each c>1/√2 admits a fixed admissible P and a finite real K such that (M P).factorCost N ≤ K LN (1/2) c N for every N≥2. P and K precede N, as required. This does not claim a single tuple attains the infimum. The stronger hLP quantification over even inadmissible P is unnecessary but can be removed by adding an admissibility guard.
- theoremRA: a supplied real-valued Fsup satisfying the interface has the rate costExpRA θ a. theoremRA_opt specialises the algebraic optimiser. Neither proves finiteness or correctness of a recursively defined algorithm.
- corollaryP: a supplied T dominated as in hport by the supplied family of rate-bounded real functions has LBound (1/2) 0 T. It supplies no computable scheduler or algorithm.
- theoremU_assembly and theoremDL_assembly: abstract recurrence/product/quotient upper-bound implications. The former does not establish the growing-degree hypothesis chain; the latter does not state the discrete-logarithm input, output, or equation being solved.

All thresholds in LBound, FM, LD, relation_supply and the final rates can depend on fixed parameters and the supplied functions. None of these statements justifies letting a single tuple depend on N, or obtaining a rate of o(1) uniform in degree/k. Conversely, the fixed-j portfolio limit does not need such uniformity. Those quantifier choices are appropriate.

The complete current hypothesis set is inconsistent because CEP alone is refutable. Passing it as a Prop argument instead of declaring an axiom preserves kernel soundness: Lean can prove a false-premise implication. It does not make that implication evidence for factoring. After repairing CEP, the moment formulations show no additional transcription contradiction in this statement audit, but their truth and a faithful semantic instantiation of the cost interfaces still require independent work.


The accepted counterexample check is recorded in [verification.log](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/leanA_1/verification.log). To reproduce from the leanA directory, run:

    lake env lean ../codex/scratch/leanA_1/RepositoryCounterexample.lean

